			<div class="content" id="post-content-4701010">
									

<p>The execution is good overall - I mostly agree with Dr Fullham, though, in that a couple points don't make sense.</p>
<p>Why does it need to be a d-class finger? And why <em>in the world</em> would they ever order a d class to deliberately consume some of an SCP? It seems like the Foundation is running away with the idiot ball here. It would make far more sense to me if the d-class was simply careless - perhaps she tries to squish some of them without orders, and later gets sick as described. Review of the footage determines she picked her nose on the way back to the cell. Something like that.</p>
<p>I dunno, I did like the concept behind the SCP but the lack of logic in how the d-class gets contaminated leads me to a no-vote.</p>

