<p>Hey there!</p>
<p>Thanks <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1989312&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1593224620" alt="Doctor Fullham" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1989312)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doctor-fullham" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1989312); return false;">Doctor Fullham</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/andrewobt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4115020); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4115020&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1593224620" alt="AndrewOBT" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4115020)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/andrewobt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4115020); return false;">AndrewOBT</a></span> for your additional comments.</p>
<p>To me, the decision to involve the D-class was deliberate on behalf of the Foundation - in my headcanon, we're all cruel bastards who'd like nothing more than to unlock the secrets of the universe (or in this case, the micro-verse). D-class have also, for the longest time, been seen as expendable by the Foundation, so I didn't see anything illogical about abusing their involvement in this case.</p>
<p>Thanks so much for reading!</p>

