														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4737936">
									

<p>Okay, microbe civilization fighting each other ala the North and the South curing the American Civil war is pretty neat. Not the first time the idea has been done, but it's hard to be 100% original on a site with literal thousands of stories. Then the D class is instructed to touch the SCP, and to then further lick the residue? That just doesn't make any sense. Also, just how did the SCP come to the foundations notice? Where are the event logs of when they found these apparently sentient microbes in a random water sample?</p>
<p>Tl;Dr - Good base, but needs more work.</p>
<p>Also, why is this rated as Safe? Aren't sentient SCPs a minimum of Euclid? Especially since they appear to be actively hostile/dangerous, and even attempted to build a tower after noticing that they were being watched.</p>

							</div>

								
